   "en": "A table is model-ready for a question when it has one row per thing you predict, every cell a value its column allows, no unexplained holes, every column a number the model can read, and the same columns next month. listings_raw.csv fails all five: 503 rows describe 480 flats, and get_dummies produces 266 columns for 503 rows.",
